Chapter: MemoryMap

 The x86-64 identity map, stated once for the code generator that builds
 the page tables and for every driver that runs under them.

Section: RAM

  bare-metal-ram-size : Integer = 3221225472

  bare-metal-pd-count : Integer = (bare-metal-ram-size + 1073741823) / 1073741824

Section: The Device Window

 One gigabyte-sized page directory sits at page-directory index
 bare-metal-pd-count, so the window is that index's gigabyte and not the
 gigabyte after bare-metal-ram-size. The two coincide only when RAM is a
 whole number of gigabytes, which is why a ram-size derivation looks
 right at 3 GB and is not one.

 A memory BAR outside this window has two fates and neither is an error
 the driver sees at the point of the mistake. Above it nothing is mapped
 and the first register read faults. Below it the address is mapped as
 ordinary RAM inside the arena alloc-bytes hands out, so the driver and
 the heap point at the same bytes and nothing faults at all.

  bare-metal-device-window-lo : Integer = bare-metal-pd-count * 1073741824

  bare-metal-device-window-hi : Integer = (bare-metal-pd-count + 1) * 1073741824
